PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L05U1.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":5,"cefr":"B1a","unit":1,"theme":"Who Am I?","essential_question":"What makes each person unique?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1","title":"Meet Noura: Present Simple vs Present Continuous","objectives":["Students will be able to use the present simple for habits and permanent facts and the present continuous for actions happening now or around now.","Students will be able to keep state verbs (know, like, belong, want) in the simple form.","I can say what I usually do and what I'm doing these days.","I can use \"I know\" and \"I like\" (not \"I'm knowing\")."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام المضارع البسيط للعادات والحقائق الدائمة والمضارع المستمر لما يحدث الآن أو في هذه الفترة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من إبقاء أفعال الحالة (know وlike وbelong وwant) في صيغة البسيط.","أستطيع أن أقول ما أفعله عادة وما أفعله هذه الأيام.","أستطيع أن أستخدم I know وI like (وليس I'm knowing)."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"personality","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpɝsəˈnælɪti/","definition":"the way a person usually thinks, feels and behaves","arabic":"شخصية","example":"Lina has a warm and friendly personality.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-W01"},{"word":"confident","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkɑnfədənt/","definition":"sure of yourself and your abilities","arabic":"واثق من نفسه","example":"Saad looks confident when he speaks in public.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-W02"},{"word":"shy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ʃaɪ/","definition":"nervous about talking to people you don't know","arabic":"خجول","example":"My little brother is shy with new people.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-W03"},{"word":"curious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkjʊriəs/","definition":"wanting to know or learn about things","arabic":"فضولي / محب للمعرفة","example":"Curious students ask a lot of questions.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use the present simple for habits, routines, facts and permanent situations: I usually spend my free time reading. She knows everyone.\nUse the present continuous for actions happening now (Right now, she's helping me) or around now – temporary projects that are in progress these days: This month, I'm writing a story.\nState verbs describe feelings, thoughts and possession, not actions. We don't usually use them in the continuous: know, like, love, hate, want, need, believe, understand, belong, own, prefer, seem. I know the answer (NOT I'm knowing).\npresent simple: always, usually, often, every day, permanent facts\npresent continuous: now, right now, at the moment, this week/month, these days\nstate verbs → simple form: I understand, she belongs, we need\nDon't use state verbs in the continuous: (not: I'm wanting) → I want","examples":["My father works at a hospital in Jeddah.","This week, he's working at night.","Lina understands three languages.","Look! The baby is trying to walk.","I don't usually drink coffee, but I'm drinking one now.","Rakan wants to be an engineer.","These days, we're studying for the final exams.","Water boils at 100 degrees Celsius."],"common_errors":["✗ I am knowing the answer. → ✓ I know the answer. (know is a state verb → simple form.)","✗ She is go to school every day. → ✓ She goes to school every day. (Habit → present simple.)","✗ Look! It rains. → ✓ Look! It's raining. (Happening now → present continuous.)","✗ I'm liking this book very much. → ✓ I like this book very much. (like is a state verb.)"],"arabic":"المضارع البسيط للعادات والحقائق والأوضاع الدائمة: I usually spend my free time reading.\nالمضارع المستمر لما يحدث الآن أو في هذه الفترة المؤقتة: This month, I'm writing a story.\nأفعال الحالة (know وlike وwant وbelong وunderstand) لا تأتي عادة في المستمر: I know (وليس I'm knowing).\nانتبه: نقول Look! It's raining لأن الحدث يقع الآن."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Meet Noura: Present Simple vs Present Continuous”. Let’s learn present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U1-LS1 | Meet Noura: Present Simple vs Present Continuous","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Meet Noura”: My name is Noura, and I'm thirteen. People say I'm a quiet person, but I'm actually very curious – I love asking questions! Look at the green words.","on_screen":"My name is Noura, and I'm thirteen. People say I'm a quiet person, but I'm actually very curious – I love asking questions!","visual":"Image GV-L05-U1-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use the present simple for habits, routines, facts and permanent situations: I usually spend my free time reading. She knows everyone. Use the present continuous for actions happening now (Right now, she's helping me) or around now – temporary projects that are in progress these days: This month, I'm writing a story.","on_screen":"present simple: always, usually, often, every day, permanent facts • present continuous: now, right now, at the moment, this week/month, these days • state verbs → simple form: I understand, she belongs, we need","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My father works at a hospital in Jeddah. This week, he's working at night. Lina understands three languages.","on_screen":"My father works at a hospital in Jeddah. / This week, he's working at night. / Lina understands three languages.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I am knowing the answer.” That’s not right. We say: “I know the answer.” know is a state verb → simple form.","on_screen":"✗ I am knowing the answer.   ✓ I know the answer.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"This month, I'm writing a story.\" Is it finished? … Think! … No – it's in progress these days. Great job! Now you can say: I can say what I usually do and what I'm doing these days.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say what I usually do and what I'm doing these days.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","المضارع البسيط للعادات والحقائق والأوضاع الدائمة: I usually spend my free time reading.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I am knowing the answer. — الصحيح: I know the answer.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول ما أفعله عادة وما أفعله هذه الأيام."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Meet Noura","body":"My name is Noura, and I'm thirteen. People say I'm a quiet person, but I'm actually very curious – I love asking questions!\nI usually spend my free time reading or writing stories, and I belong to the school writing club.\nThis month, I'm writing a short story about my great-grandmother, who was a pearl merchant's daughter in Jubail.\nI'm also learning to code, so I'm watching online lessons every evening.\nI don't like loud parties, but I enjoy spending time with a few close friends.\nMy best friend, Lina, is the opposite of me: she's very sociable, and she knows everyone at school!\nRight now, she's helping me with my story because she has a great sense of humor.\nWe often disagree, but we always respect each other. I think we're a good team.","word_count":135,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"My uncle ___ in a bank.","options":["is working","work","working","works"],"answer":"works","explanation":"Habit, routine, fact or permanent situation → present simple.","explanation_ar":"العادة أو الحقيقة ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"Be quiet! The baby ___.","options":["sleep","is sleeping","sleeps","is sleep"],"answer":"is sleeping","explanation":"Now or temporary (these days, this month) → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الآن أو المؤقت ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"I ___ what you mean.","options":["am understanding","understanding","understand","am understand"],"answer":"understand","explanation":"State verbs (know, like, want, belong, understand) → simple form.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"This term, we ___ about ancient Arabia.","options":["are learning","learn","learns","are learn"],"answer":"are learning","explanation":"Now or temporary (these days, this month) → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الآن أو المؤقت ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"Rakan ___ to the chess club.","options":["is belonging","belongs","belong","belonging"],"answer":"belongs","explanation":"State verbs (know, like, want, belong, understand) → simple form.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"Lina usually ___ the bus, but today she's walking.","options":["taking","take","is taking","takes"],"answer":"takes","explanation":"Look at the time signal (usually / now / these days).","explanation_ar":"انتبه لكلمة الزمن."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the present simple or the present continuous. Word bank: is repairing, plays, doesn't want","items":[{"q":"Faisal ______ (play) football every Thursday.","options":[],"answer":"plays","explanation":"Habit, routine, fact or permanent situation → present simple.","explanation_ar":"العادة أو الحقيقة ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"At the moment, my dad ______ (repair) the air conditioner.","options":[],"answer":"is repairing","explanation":"Now or temporary (these days, this month) → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الآن أو المؤقت ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"My sister ______ (not / want) a party for her birthday.","options":[],"answer":"doesn't want","explanation":"State verbs (know, like, want, belong, understand) → simple form.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"I am believing you.","options":[],"answer":"I believe you.","explanation":"am believing → believe. State verbs (know, like, want, belong, understand) → simple form.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: am believing → believe. أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"Look! Our team scores a goal!","options":[],"answer":"Look! Our team is scoring a goal!","explanation":"scores → is scoring. Now or temporary (these days, this month) → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: scores → is scoring. الآن أو المؤقت ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"The sun is rising in the east.","options":[],"answer":"The sun rises in the east.","explanation":"is rising → rises. Habit, routine, fact or permanent situation → present simple.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: is rising → rises. العادة أو الحقيقة ← المضارع البسيط."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write true sentences about you.","items":[{"q":"Something I do every weekend: ___","options":[],"answer":"I visit my grandparents every weekend.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something I'm doing these days: ___","options":[],"answer":"These days, I'm learning to play chess.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A place I belong to: ___","options":[],"answer":"I belong to the school robotics club.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something I don't usually do, but I'm doing it this week: ___","options":[],"answer":"I don't usually get up at five, but this week I'm getting up early for exams.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something I really want: ___","options":[],"answer":"I really want a telescope.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write a mini-profile.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your permanent habits and likes.","options":[],"answer":"I live in Taif with my family. I usually read before bed. I love football.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about what you are doing these days.","options":[],"answer":"This month, I'm preparing for a competition. I'm learning new words every day. I'm also helping my brother with math.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Interview a partner. Write 2 sentences (one simple, one continuous).","options":[],"answer":"Saad usually plays tennis. This month, he's training for a match.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Ball Toss Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Students stand in a circle. The teacher says a cue word and throws the ball.","The catcher makes a sentence with the cue word and present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs.","If it is correct, the catcher chooses the next cue word and throws the ball to a new student.","If it is not correct, classmates help fix it, and the same student tries again."],"data":[{"label":"I usually…"},{"label":"Right now, I'm…"},{"label":"I don't usually… but today I'm…"},{"label":"She always…"},{"label":"These days, he's…"},{"label":"I know…"},{"label":"I belong to…"},{"label":"My English is getting…"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My grandmother ___ every morning after Fajr.","options":["is walking","walks","walking","walk"],"answer":"walks","explanation":"Habit, routine, fact or permanent situation → present simple.","explanation_ar":"العادة أو الحقيقة ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"Listen! My phone ___ in my bag.","options":["rings","is ring","ring","is ringing"],"answer":"is ringing","explanation":"Now or temporary (these days, this month) → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الآن أو المؤقت ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"Do you ___ the answer to question 5?","options":["are knowing","knowing","know","knows"],"answer":"know","explanation":"State verbs (know, like, want, belong, understand) → simple form.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"These days, my brother ___ for his driving test.","options":["is practice","practice","practices","is practicing"],"answer":"is practicing","explanation":"Now or temporary (these days, this month) → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الآن أو المؤقت ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["Our school starts at seven.","Our school is starting at seven every day.","Our school start at seven.","Our school is start at seven."],"answer":"Our school starts at seven.","explanation":"Habit, routine, fact or permanent situation → present simple.","explanation_ar":"العادة أو الحقيقة ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["I am need a new charger.","I needing a new charger.","I need a new charger.","I'm needing a new charger."],"answer":"I need a new charger.","explanation":"State verbs (know, like, want, belong, understand) → simple form.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["What do you read at the moment?","What are you reading at the moment?","What you are reading at the moment?","What are you read at the moment?"],"answer":"What are you reading at the moment?","explanation":"Now or temporary (these days, this month) → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الآن أو المؤقت ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"Water ___ at 0 degrees Celsius.","options":["is freeze","freezes","freeze","is freezing"],"answer":"freezes","explanation":"Habit, routine, fact or permanent situation → present simple.","explanation_ar":"العادة أو الحقيقة ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["My parents are owning a small farm.","My parents owning a small farm.","My parents owns a small farm.","My parents own a small farm."],"answer":"My parents own a small farm.","explanation":"State verbs (know, like, want, belong, understand) → simple form.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"He usually wears a thobe, but today he ___ a suit.","options":["is wearing","wear","wears","is wear"],"answer":"is wearing","explanation":"Look at the time signal (usually / now / these days).","explanation_ar":"انتبه لكلمة الزمن."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Noura at her desk with a notebook and a laptop showing an online coding lesson, a family photo of her great-grandmother on the wall, and her sociable friend Lina laughing beside her. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Noura at her desk with a notebook and a laptop showing an online coding lesson, a family photo of her great-grandmother on the wall, and her sociable friend Lina laughing beside her"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now)"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows personality (the way a person usually thinks, feels and behaves); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing personality: the way a person usually thinks, feels and behaves"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows confident (sure of yourself and your abilities); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing confident: sure of yourself and your abilities"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows shy (nervous about talking to people you don't know); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing shy: nervous about talking to people you don't know"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows curious (wanting to know or learn about things); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing curious: wanting to know or learn about things"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Ball Toss Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Ball Toss Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-W01","script":"personality. personality. Lina has a warm and friendly personality.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-W02","script":"confident. confident. Saad looks confident when he speaks in public.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-W03","script":"shy. shy. My little brother is shy with new people.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-W04","script":"curious. curious. Curious students ask a lot of questions.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-T1","script":"My name is Noura, and I'm thirteen. People say I'm a quiet person, but I'm actually very curious – I love asking questions! I usually spend my free time reading or writing stories, and I belong to the school writing club. This month, I'm writing a short story about my great-grandmother, who was a pearl merchant's daughter in Jubail. I'm also learning to code, so I'm watching online lessons every evening. I don't like loud parties, but I enjoy spending time with a few close friends. My best friend, Lina, is the opposite of me: she's very sociable, and she knows everyone at school! Right now, she's helping me with my story because she has a great sense of humor. We often disagree, but we always respect each other. I think we're a good team.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Meet Noura: Present Simple vs Present Continuous”. Let’s learn present simple (habits, facts, permanent situations) vs present continuous (now, around now); state verbs together. Listen to the start of “Meet Noura”: My name is Noura, and I'm thirteen. People say I'm a quiet person, but I'm actually very curious – I love asking questions! Look at the green words. Use the present simple for habits, routines, facts and permanent situations: I usually spend my free time reading. She knows everyone. Use the present continuous for actions happening now (Right now, she's helping me) or around now – temporary projects that are in progress these days: This month, I'm writing a story. Here are some examples. My father works at a hospital in Jeddah. This week, he's working at night. Lina understands three languages. Be careful! Some learners say: “I am knowing the answer.” That’s not right. We say: “I know the answer.” know is a state verb → simple form. Quick check: \"This month, I'm writing a story.\" Is it finished? … Think! … No – it's in progress these days. Great job! Now you can say: I can say what I usually do and what I'm doing these days.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2","title":"He's Always Borrowing My Pens! Temporary, Changing and Annoying","objectives":["Students will be able to contrast permanent situations (present simple) with temporary ones (present continuous).","Students will be able to use always + -ing for annoying habits and choose the right form of think and have.","I can say \"I live in Taif, but I'm staying in Abha this week.\"","I can complain: \"He's always borrowing my pens!\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من المقارنة بين الأوضاع الدائمة (المضارع البسيط) والمؤقتة (المضارع المستمر).","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام always + ing للعادات المزعجة واختيار الصيغة الصحيحة لـ think وhave.","أستطيع أن أقول I live in Taif, but I'm staying in Abha this week.","أستطيع أن أشتكي: He's always borrowing my pens!"],"vocabulary":[{"word":"honest","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɑnəst/","definition":"always telling the truth","arabic":"صادق / أمين","example":"An honest person doesn't cheat.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS2-W01"},{"word":"patient","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpeɪʃənt/","definition":"able to wait calmly without getting angry","arabic":"صبور","example":"A good teacher is patient with every student.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS2-W02"},{"word":"reliable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/rɪˈlaɪəbəl/","definition":"someone you can trust to do what they say","arabic":"يُعتمد عليه","example":"Ziyad is reliable – he's never late.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS2-W03"},{"word":"ambitious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/æmˈbɪʃəs/","definition":"wanting very much to succeed","arabic":"طموح","example":"Rakan is ambitious; he wants to be a surgeon.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Temporary situations use the present continuous; permanent ones use the present simple: My dad works in Riyadh (permanent), but this month he's working in Dammam (temporary).\nChanging situations use the present continuous with verbs like get, become, grow, improve: My English is getting better. The city is growing fast.\nalways + present continuous shows an annoying habit: My brother is always borrowing my pens! Some verbs have two meanings: I think you're right (opinion – simple) / I'm thinking about the trip (considering – continuous); We have a car (own – simple) / We're having lunch (eating – continuous).","examples":["We usually live in Taif, but this summer we're living in Abha.","My little sister is growing so fast!","Prices are going up these days.","My cousin is always losing his keys!","What do you think of the new library? – I think it's great.","I'm thinking of learning Japanese.","We have three cats.","Shh! Grandpa is having a nap."],"common_errors":["✗ I'm thinking you are right. → ✓ I think you are right. (Opinion → simple.)","✗ My brother always borrows my things! (complaint) → ✓ My brother is always borrowing my things! (Annoying habit → always + -ing.)","✗ My English gets better these days. → ✓ My English is getting better these days. (Changing situation → continuous.)","✗ We are having a big garden. → ✓ We have a big garden. (have = own → simple.)"],"arabic":"الوضع المؤقت بالمضارع المستمر والدائم بالبسيط: My dad works in Riyadh, but this month he's working in Dammam.\nالأوضاع المتغيرة بالمستمر مع get وbecome وgrow: My English is getting better.\nalways + المستمر للعادة المزعجة: He's always borrowing my pens!\nthink للرأي بالبسيط (I think…) وللتفكير في أمر بالمستمر (I'm thinking about…)، وhave للملكية بالبسيط وللأكل والتجربة بالمستمر."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “He's Always Borrowing My Pens! Temporary, Changing and Annoying”. Let’s learn present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have) together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U1-LS2 | He's Always Borrowing My Pens! Temporary, Changing and Annoying","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: I'm staying with my cousins this week. • The weather is getting cooler. He isn't living at home this year; he's at university. Are you thinking about joining the club? • What do you think of my story?","on_screen":"I'm staying with my cousins this week. • The weather is getting cooler. | He isn't living at home this year; he's at university. | Are you thinking about joining the club? • What do you think of my story?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Temporary situations use the present continuous; permanent ones use the present simple: My dad works in Riyadh (permanent), but this month he's working in Dammam (temporary). Changing situations use the present continuous with verbs like get, become, grow, improve: My English is getting better. The city is growing fast.","on_screen":"present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. We usually live in Taif, but this summer we're living in Abha. My little sister is growing so fast! Prices are going up these days.","on_screen":"We usually live in Taif, but this summer we're living in Abha. / My little sister is growing so fast! / Prices are going up these days.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I'm thinking you are right.” That’s not right. We say: “I think you are right.” Opinion → simple.","on_screen":"✗ I'm thinking you are right.   ✓ I think you are right.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"He's always borrowing my pens!\" Is the speaker happy about it? … Think! … No – it's annoying. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I live in Taif, but I'm staying in Abha this week.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"I live in Taif, but I'm staying in Abha this week.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الوضع المؤقت بالمضارع المستمر والدائم بالبسيط: My dad works in Riyadh, but this month he's working in Dammam.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I'm thinking you are right. — الصحيح: I think you are right.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول I live in Taif, but I'm staying in Abha this week."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"My cousin usually lives in Riyadh, but this year he ___ in London.","options":["studies","studying","study","is studying"],"answer":"is studying","explanation":"Temporary situation → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الوضع المؤقت ← المستمر."},{"q":"Our town ___ very quickly. There are new buildings everywhere.","options":["grows","grow","is growing","growing"],"answer":"is growing","explanation":"Changing situation (getting, becoming, growing) → continuous.","explanation_ar":"التغيّر ← المستمر."},{"q":"My brother ___ my phone without asking!","options":["always takes","is always taking","always take","is always take"],"answer":"is always taking","explanation":"always + -ing = annoying habit.","explanation_ar":"always + ing للعادة المزعجة."},{"q":"I ___ this film is boring.","options":["am thinking","thinking","thinks","think"],"answer":"think","explanation":"think = opinion (simple) / considering (continuous).","explanation_ar":"think بمعنيين."},{"q":"We ___ dinner right now. Can I call you later?","options":["having","are having","have","has"],"answer":"are having","explanation":"have = own (simple) / eat, take, enjoy (continuous).","explanation_ar":"have بمعنيين."},{"q":"The Earth ___ around the sun.","options":["goes","go","going","is going"],"answer":"goes","explanation":"Permanent situation → present simple.","explanation_ar":"الوضع الدائم ← البسيط."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the present simple or the present continuous. Word bank: is getting, am thinking, have","items":[{"q":"I ______ (think) about joining the debate club.","options":[],"answer":"am thinking","explanation":"think = opinion (simple) / considering (continuous).","explanation_ar":"think بمعنيين."},{"q":"My grandparents ______ (have) a farm in Al-Ahsa.","options":[],"answer":"have","explanation":"have = own (simple) / eat, take, enjoy (continuous).","explanation_ar":"have بمعنيين."},{"q":"It ______ (get) dark. Let's go home.","options":[],"answer":"is getting","explanation":"Changing situation (getting, becoming, growing) → continuous.","explanation_ar":"التغيّر ← المستمر."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Rewrite as a complaint with always.","items":[{"q":"My sister interrupts me.  (complaint)","options":[],"answer":"My sister is always interrupting me!","explanation":"always + -ing = annoying habit.","explanation_ar":"always + ing للعادة المزعجة."},{"q":"The neighbors play loud music.  (complaint)","options":[],"answer":"The neighbors are always playing loud music!","explanation":"always + -ing = annoying habit.","explanation_ar":"always + ing للعادة المزعجة."},{"q":"You forget your homework.  (complaint)","options":[],"answer":"You're always forgetting your homework!","explanation":"always + -ing = annoying habit.","explanation_ar":"always + ing للعادة المزعجة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your life now.","items":[{"q":"Something permanent about my family: ___","options":[],"answer":"My family lives in a house near the mosque.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something temporary in my life these days: ___","options":[],"answer":"These days, I'm sleeping early because of exams.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something that is changing in my town: ___","options":[],"answer":"My town is getting busier every year.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something annoying that someone is always doing: ___","options":[],"answer":"My little brother is always taking my snacks!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something I'm thinking about doing: ___","options":[],"answer":"I'm thinking about learning to swim properly.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Then vs these days.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences: what a person usually does and what he's doing differently this month.","options":[],"answer":"My dad usually drives to work. This month, he's walking because his car is at the garage.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences about things that are getting better or worse.","options":[],"answer":"My handwriting is getting neater. The traffic is getting worse.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your opinion of a book or film with \"I think…\" and a plan with \"I'm thinking of…\".","options":[],"answer":"I think the film was exciting. I'm thinking of reading the book.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Dice Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Turn over a cue card and roll the die.","Make a sentence with the cue in the form shown by the die.","The player on the left checks; a correct sentence wins the card.","The player with the most cards after 7 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"She / usually / walk to school / today / take the bus"},{"cue":"I / know / the answer / state verb"},{"cue":"He / always / borrow my pens / annoying"},{"cue":"My brother / live / in Riyadh / permanent"},{"cue":"This week / my cousin / stay with us / temporary"},{"cue":"I / think / you're right / opinion"},{"cue":"I / think / about the trip / considering"},{"cue":"We / have / a big house / own"},{"cue":"We / have / lunch now / activity"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My dad normally works in Taif, but this week he ___ in Jeddah.","options":["work","working","is working","works"],"answer":"is working","explanation":"Temporary situation → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الوضع المؤقت ← المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["The weather is getting colder.","The weather getting colder.","The weather is get colder.","The weather gets colder these days now."],"answer":"The weather is getting colder.","explanation":"Changing situation (getting, becoming, growing) → continuous.","explanation_ar":"التغيّر ← المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["You always are leaving the door open!","You're leaving always the door open!","You're always leaving the door open!","You're always leave the door open!"],"answer":"You're always leaving the door open!","explanation":"always + -ing = annoying habit.","explanation_ar":"always + ing للعادة المزعجة."},{"q":"What do you ___ of my new haircut?","options":["thinks","think","thinking","are thinking"],"answer":"think","explanation":"think = opinion (simple) / considering (continuous).","explanation_ar":"think بمعنيين."},{"q":"","options":["My uncle has two cars.","My uncle having two cars.","My uncle have two cars.","My uncle is having two cars."],"answer":"My uncle has two cars.","explanation":"have = own (simple) / eat, take, enjoy (continuous).","explanation_ar":"have بمعنيين."},{"q":"","options":["Lina is have a great time in Abha.","Lina is having a great time in Abha.","Lina having a great time in Abha.","Lina has a great time in Abha right now."],"answer":"Lina is having a great time in Abha.","explanation":"have = own (simple) / eat, take, enjoy (continuous).","explanation_ar":"have بمعنيين."},{"q":"My brother usually ___ coffee, but he's drinking tea today.","options":["is drinking","drink","drinking","drinks"],"answer":"drinks","explanation":"Permanent situation → present simple.","explanation_ar":"الوضع الدائم ← البسيط."},{"q":"","options":["I'm think of buying a new bike.","I thinking of buying a new bike.","I think of buying a new bike now.","I'm thinking of buying a new bike."],"answer":"I'm thinking of buying a new bike.","explanation":"think = opinion (simple) / considering (continuous).","explanation_ar":"think بمعنيين."},{"q":"My sister ___ taller every month!","options":["getting","get","is getting","gets"],"answer":"is getting","explanation":"Changing situation (getting, becoming, growing) → continuous.","explanation_ar":"التغيّر ← المستمر."},{"q":"Which sentence is a complaint?","options":["\"He's eating a sandwich now.\"","\"He eats a sandwich every day.\"","\"He always eats breakfast.\"","\"He's always eating my sandwiches!\""],"answer":"\"He's always eating my sandwiches!\"","explanation":"always + -ing = annoying habit.","explanation_ar":"always + ing للعادة المزعجة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Two brothers sharing a desk: the younger one taking pens from his brother's pencil case again, the older one rolling his eyes; a calendar marks \"Visiting Abha – this week\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two brothers sharing a desk: the younger one taking pens from his brother's pencil case again, the older one rolling his eyes; a calendar marks \"Visiting Abha – this week\""},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have): a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Who Am I?”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing)"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows honest (always telling the truth); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing honest: always telling the truth"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows patient (able to wait calmly without getting angry); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing patient: able to wait calmly without getting angry"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows reliable (someone you can trust to do what they say); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing reliable: someone you can trust to do what they say"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows ambitious (wanting very much to succeed); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing ambitious: wanting very much to succeed"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Dice Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Dice Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS2-W01","script":"honest. honest. An honest person doesn't cheat.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS2-W02","script":"patient. patient. A good teacher is patient with every student.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS2-W03","script":"reliable. reliable. Ziyad is reliable – he's never late.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS2-W04","script":"ambitious. ambitious. Rakan is ambitious; he wants to be a surgeon.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “He's Always Borrowing My Pens! Temporary, Changing and Annoying”. Let’s learn present continuous for temporary situations, changing situations and annoying habits (always + -ing); verbs with two meanings (think, have) together. Remember these patterns: I'm staying with my cousins this week. • The weather is getting cooler. He isn't living at home this year; he's at university. Are you thinking about joining the club? • What do you think of my story? Temporary situations use the present continuous; permanent ones use the present simple: My dad works in Riyadh (permanent), but this month he's working in Dammam (temporary). Changing situations use the present continuous with verbs like get, become, grow, improve: My English is getting better. The city is growing fast. Here are some examples. We usually live in Taif, but this summer we're living in Abha. My little sister is growing so fast! Prices are going up these days. Be careful! Some learners say: “I'm thinking you are right.” That’s not right. We say: “I think you are right.” Opinion → simple. Quick check: \"He's always borrowing my pens!\" Is the speaker happy about it? … Think! … No – it's annoying. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"I live in Taif, but I'm staying in Abha this week.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3","title":"Confident, Curious, Reliable: Personality Words with un-, in-, im-, dis-","objectives":["Students will be able to describe people with a range of personality adjectives.","Students will be able to form opposites with the prefixes un-, in-, im- and dis-.","I can describe my personality and my friends' personalities.","I can make opposites like \"impatient\" and \"dishonest\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من وصف الأشخاص بمجموعة من صفات الشخصية.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين الأضداد بالبادئات un- وin- وim- وdis-.","أستطيع أن أصف شخصيتي وشخصيات أصدقائي.","أستطيع أن أكوّن أضدادًا مثل impatient وdishonest."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"sociable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsoʊʃəbəl/","definition":"enjoying being with other people","arabic":"اجتماعي","example":"Sociable people make friends easily.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W01"},{"word":"creative","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/kriˈeɪtɪv/","definition":"good at making new things and ideas","arabic":"مبدع","example":"Noura is creative – she writes amazing stories.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W02"},{"word":"calm","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/kɑm/","definition":"quiet and not worried or angry","arabic":"هادئ","example":"Stay calm and read the question again.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W03"},{"word":"stubborn","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈstʌbɚn/","definition":"not willing to change your mind","arabic":"عنيد","example":"My grandpa is stubborn about his old phone.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W04"},{"word":"sense of humor","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/sɛns ʌv ˈhjumɚ/","definition":"the ability to see and enjoy funny things","arabic":"حس الفكاهة","example":"Adam has a great sense of humor.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W05"},{"word":"character","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɛrɪktɚ/","definition":"the qualities that make a person who they are","arabic":"طبع / شخصية","example":"Helping others shows good character.","image_id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W06","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W06"}],"explanation":{"text":"Personality adjectives describe character: confident, shy, curious, honest, patient, reliable, ambitious, sociable, creative, calm, stubborn.\nMany personality opposites use a prefix: un- (unfriendly, unreliable, unkind), in- (insensitive, inconsiderate), im- before p and m (impatient, impolite, immature), dis- (dishonest, disorganized, disrespectful).\nLearn each word with its prefix – there is no simple rule for un- or in-. But im- usually comes before p or m.\nCollocations/phrases: un-: friendly → unfriendly • reliable → unreliable • kind → unkind • selfish → unselfish | in-: sensitive → insensitive • considerate → inconsiderate • dependent → independent | im- (before p/m): patient → impatient • polite → impolite • mature → immature | dis-: honest → dishonest • organized → disorganized • respectful → disrespectful","examples":["Saad is confident in front of an audience.","My cousin is a bit shy at first.","Don't be impatient – the bus will come.","Cheating is dishonest.","Lina is sociable; she talks to everyone.","A reliable friend always keeps his promises.","My desk is messy because I'm disorganized.","It's impolite to look at your phone during a conversation."],"common_errors":["✗ He is very unpatient. → ✓ He is very impatient. (patient → impatient.)","✗ She is unhonest. → ✓ She is dishonest. (honest → dishonest.)","✗ My brother is very social. He has many friends. → ✓ My brother is very sociable. (sociable = enjoys people.)","✗ He has a good humor. → ✓ He has a good sense of humor. (sense of humor.)"],"arabic":"صفات الشخصية: confident (واثق) وcurious (فضولي) وreliable (يُعتمد عليه) وambitious (طموح) وsociable (اجتماعي).\nنكوّن الأضداد بالبادئات: un (unfriendly) وin (insensitive) وim قبل p وm (impatient) وdis (dishonest).\nنقول impatient وليس unpatient، وdishonest وليس unhonest."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Confident, Curious, Reliable: Personality Words with un-, in-, im-, dis-”. Let’s learn personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis- together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U1-LS3 | Confident, Curious, Reliable: Personality Words with un-, in-, im-, dis-","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. sociable: enjoying being with other people. creative: good at making new things and ideas. calm: quiet and not worried or angry.","on_screen":"sociable | creative | calm","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Personality adjectives describe character: confident, shy, curious, honest, patient, reliable, ambitious, sociable, creative, calm, stubborn. Many personality opposites use a prefix: un- (unfriendly, unreliable, unkind), in- (insensitive, inconsiderate), im- before p and m (impatient, impolite, immature), dis- (dishonest, disorganized, disrespectful).","on_screen":"personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis-","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Saad is confident in front of an audience. My cousin is a bit shy at first. Don't be impatient – the bus will come.","on_screen":"Saad is confident in front of an audience. / My cousin is a bit shy at first. / Don't be impatient – the bus will come.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He is very unpatient.” That’s not right. We say: “He is very impatient.” patient → impatient.","on_screen":"✗ He is very unpatient.   ✓ He is very impatient.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Which prefix goes with \"polite\"? … Think! … *im-* – impolite. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe my personality and my friends' personalities.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can describe my personality and my friends' personalities.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis-.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","صفات الشخصية: confident (واثق) وcurious (فضولي) وreliable (يُعتمد عليه) وambitious (طموح) وsociable (اجتماعي).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He is very unpatient. — الصحيح: He is very impatient.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أصف شخصيتي وشخصيات أصدقائي."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"Hamad always tells the truth. He's ___.","options":["shy","stubborn","honest","creative"],"answer":"honest","explanation":"Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"Rakan wants to be the best surgeon in the country. He's ___.","options":["shy","impolite","calm","ambitious"],"answer":"ambitious","explanation":"Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"The opposite of \"patient\" is ___.","options":["dispatient","impatient","inpatient","unpatient"],"answer":"impatient","explanation":"im- before p or m (impatient, impolite).","explanation_ar":"im قبل p وm."},{"q":"The opposite of \"organized\" is ___.","options":["disorganized","imorganized","unorganized","inorganized"],"answer":"disorganized","explanation":"dis- + adjective (dishonest, disorganized).","explanation_ar":"البادئة dis."},{"q":"My cousin never does what he promises. He's ___.","options":["unreliable","disreliable","imreliable","inreliable"],"answer":"unreliable","explanation":"un- + adjective.","explanation_ar":"البادئة un."},{"q":"People who don't think about others' feelings are ___.","options":["unsensitive","dissensitive","imsensitive","insensitive"],"answer":"insensitive","explanation":"in- + adjective (insensitive, inconsiderate).","explanation_ar":"البادئة in."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the person to the adjective.","items":[{"q":"She makes beautiful paintings and new games.","options":["sociable","creative","shy","curious","stubborn","calm"],"answer":"creative","explanation":"She makes beautiful paintings and new games. → creative. Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"He never gets angry, even in traffic.","options":["sociable","creative","shy","curious","stubborn","calm"],"answer":"calm","explanation":"He never gets angry, even in traffic. → calm. Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"She asks \"why?\" about everything.","options":["sociable","creative","shy","curious","stubborn","calm"],"answer":"curious","explanation":"She asks \"why?\" about everything. → curious. Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"He won't change his mind.","options":["sociable","creative","shy","curious","stubborn","calm"],"answer":"stubborn","explanation":"He won't change his mind. → stubborn. Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"She loves parties and meeting people.","options":["sociable","creative","shy","curious","stubborn","calm"],"answer":"sociable","explanation":"She loves parties and meeting people. → sociable. Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"He feels nervous with new people.","options":["sociable","creative","shy","curious","stubborn","calm"],"answer":"shy","explanation":"He feels nervous with new people. → shy. Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Describe people you know.","items":[{"q":"My best friend is ___ because ___.","options":[],"answer":"My best friend is reliable because he always keeps his promises.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I am ___ but sometimes I'm ___.","options":[],"answer":"I am calm, but sometimes I'm impatient.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A creative person in my family is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A creative person in my family is my aunt; she designs dresses.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"It's impolite to ___.","options":[],"answer":"It's impolite to interrupt older people.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Someone with a great sense of humor is ___.","options":[],"answer":"Someone with a great sense of humor is my uncle Fahad.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: My personality profile.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 adjectives that describe you, with a reason for each.","options":[],"answer":"I'm curious – I love science. I'm sociable – I have many friends. I'm a bit stubborn. I'm reliable – I'm never late.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 things you want to change about your personality using a prefix word.","options":[],"answer":"I don't want to be impatient. I want to be less disorganized.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about a hero's character.","options":[],"answer":"A hero is brave, honest and unselfish.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis- correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Vocabulary Bingo","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Students write nine words from the list in their grid.","The teacher (or a student caller) reads a definition or Arabic meaning.","Students cross out the matching word.","Three in a row = \"Bingo!\" The winner must read the words and say what each means."],"data":[{"word":"personality","match":"the way a person usually thinks, feels and behaves","arabic":"شخصية"},{"word":"confident","match":"sure of yourself and your abilities","arabic":"واثق من نفسه"},{"word":"shy","match":"nervous about talking to people you don't know","arabic":"خجول"},{"word":"curious","match":"wanting to know or learn about things","arabic":"فضولي / محب للمعرفة"},{"word":"honest","match":"always telling the truth","arabic":"صادق / أمين"},{"word":"patient","match":"able to wait calmly without getting angry","arabic":"صبور"},{"word":"reliable","match":"someone you can trust to do what they say","arabic":"يُعتمد عليه"},{"word":"ambitious","match":"wanting very much to succeed","arabic":"طموح"},{"word":"sociable","match":"enjoying being with other people","arabic":"اجتماعي"},{"word":"creative","match":"good at making new things and ideas","arabic":"مبدع"},{"word":"calm","match":"quiet and not worried or angry","arabic":"هادئ"},{"word":"stubborn","match":"not willing to change your mind","arabic":"عنيد"},{"word":"sense of humor","match":"the ability to see and enjoy funny things","arabic":"حس الفكاهة"},{"word":"character","match":"the qualities that make a person who they are","arabic":"طبع / شخصية"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Faisal is never late and always does his work. He's ___.","options":["stubborn","dishonest","shy","reliable"],"answer":"reliable","explanation":"Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"The opposite of \"polite\" is ___.","options":["dispolite","impolite","unpolite","inpolite"],"answer":"impolite","explanation":"im- before p or m (impatient, impolite).","explanation_ar":"im قبل p وm."},{"q":"The opposite of \"friendly\" is ___.","options":["unfriendly","disfriendly","infriendly","imfriendly"],"answer":"unfriendly","explanation":"un- + adjective.","explanation_ar":"البادئة un."},{"q":"The opposite of \"respectful\" is ___.","options":["inrespectful","unrespectful","disrespectful","imrespectful"],"answer":"disrespectful","explanation":"dis- + adjective (dishonest, disorganized).","explanation_ar":"البادئة dis."},{"q":"Noura loves to learn new things. She's ___.","options":["impolite","curious","calm","stubborn"],"answer":"curious","explanation":"Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"The opposite of \"considerate\" is ___.","options":["inconsiderate","unconsiderate","imconsiderate","disconsiderate"],"answer":"inconsiderate","explanation":"in- + adjective (insensitive, inconsiderate).","explanation_ar":"البادئة in."},{"q":"","options":["My little brother is too immature for this game.","My little brother is too inmature for this game.","My little brother is too dismature for this game.","My little brother is too unmature for this game."],"answer":"My little brother is too immature for this game.","explanation":"im- before p or m (impatient, impolite).","explanation_ar":"im قبل p وm."},{"q":"Someone who enjoys funny things has a good ___.","options":["humor sense","funny sense","humor of sense","sense of humor"],"answer":"sense of humor","explanation":"Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"Adam stays ___ during exams; he never panics.","options":["shy","dishonest","stubborn","calm"],"answer":"calm","explanation":"Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"Which word means \"not honest\"?","options":["inhonest","imhonest","dishonest","unhonest"],"answer":"dishonest","explanation":"dis- + adjective (dishonest, disorganized).","explanation_ar":"البادئة dis."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A personality wheel poster with icons: a lightbulb (creative), a magnifying glass (curious), a clock (reliable), a mountain (ambitious), a smiling group (sociable) and a calm lake (calm). Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A personality wheel poster with icons: a lightbulb (creative), a magnifying glass (curious), a clock (reliable), a mountain (ambitious), a smiling group (sociable) and a calm lake (calm)"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 6 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sociable (enjoying being with other people); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sociable: enjoying being with other people"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows creative (good at making new things and ideas); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing creative: good at making new things and ideas"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows calm (quiet and not worried or angry); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing calm: quiet and not worried or angry"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows stubborn (not willing to change your mind); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing stubborn: not willing to change your mind"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sense of humor (the ability to see and enjoy funny things); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sense of humor: the ability to see and enjoy funny things"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-W06","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows character (the qualities that make a person who they are); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing character: the qualities that make a person who they are"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Vocabulary Bingo”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Vocabulary Bingo"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W01","script":"sociable. sociable. Sociable people make friends easily.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W02","script":"creative. creative. Noura is creative – she writes amazing stories.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W03","script":"calm. calm. Stay calm and read the question again.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W04","script":"stubborn. stubborn. My grandpa is stubborn about his old phone.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W05","script":"sense of humor. sense of humor. Adam has a great sense of humor.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-W06","script":"character. character. Helping others shows good character.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Confident, Curious, Reliable: Personality Words with un-, in-, im-, dis-”. Let’s learn personality adjectives; negative prefixes un-, in-, im-, dis- together. Meet some new words. sociable: enjoying being with other people. creative: good at making new things and ideas. calm: quiet and not worried or angry. Personality adjectives describe character: confident, shy, curious, honest, patient, reliable, ambitious, sociable, creative, calm, stubborn. Many personality opposites use a prefix: un- (unfriendly, unreliable, unkind), in- (insensitive, inconsiderate), im- before p and m (impatient, impolite, immature), dis- (dishonest, disorganized, disrespectful). Here are some examples. Saad is confident in front of an audience. My cousin is a bit shy at first. Don't be impatient – the bus will come. Be careful! Some learners say: “He is very unpatient.” That’s not right. We say: “He is very impatient.” patient → impatient. Quick check: Which prefix goes with \"polite\"? … Think! … *im-* – impolite. Great job! Now you can say: I can describe my personality and my friends' personalities.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS4","title":"Too Many Ideas in One Sentence: Fixing Run-On Sentences","objectives":["Students will be able to identify run-on sentences and comma splices.","Students will be able to fix run-ons in three ways: a period, a comma + and/but/so, or a word like because/when.","I can find run-on sentences in my writing.","I can fix them with a period, a comma + conjunction, or because."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التعرف على الجمل المتصلة الخاطئة وجمل الفاصلة الخاطئة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تصحيحها بثلاث طرق: النقطة، أو الفاصلة مع أداة ربط، أو كلمة مثل because وwhen.","أستطيع أن أجد الجمل المتصلة الخاطئة في كتابتي.","أستطيع أن أصححها بالنقطة أو الفاصلة مع أداة ربط أو because."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"personality","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpɝsəˈnælɪti/","definition":"the way a person usually thinks, feels and behaves","arabic":"شخصية","example":"Lina has a warm and friendly personality.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"confident","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkɑnfədənt/","definition":"sure of yourself and your abilities","arabic":"واثق من نفسه","example":"Saad looks confident when he speaks in public.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"shy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ʃaɪ/","definition":"nervous about talking to people you don't know","arabic":"خجول","example":"My little brother is shy with new people.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"curious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkjʊriəs/","definition":"wanting to know or learn about things","arabic":"فضولي / محب للمعرفة","example":"Curious students ask a lot of questions.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"honest","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɑnəst/","definition":"always telling the truth","arabic":"صادق / أمين","example":"An honest person doesn't cheat.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"patient","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpeɪʃənt/","definition":"able to wait calmly without getting angry","arabic":"صبور","example":"A good teacher is patient with every student.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A run-on sentence joins two complete sentences with no punctuation: (not: I love reading I read every night.) A comma splice joins them with only a comma: (not: I love reading, I read every night.) Both are mistakes.\nFix 1 – make two sentences: I love reading. I read every night. Fix 2 – comma + and/but/or/so: I love reading, so I read every night. Fix 3 – use a joining word like because, when, although, if: I read every night because I love reading.\nArabic writing often joins many ideas with و (and) in one long sentence. In English, keep sentences clear and short, and check that each sentence has one main idea or is joined correctly.\nRun-on: two sentences with no punctuation → wrong\nComma splice: two sentences with only a comma → wrong\nFix: period • comma + and/but/or/so • because/when/although/if\nEach complete sentence needs a subject and a verb.","examples":["Lina is cheerful. She smiles all the time.","Rakan is shy, but he is very funny with his friends.","I stayed home because I was sick.","My brother is ambitious, so he studies every day.","When I feel nervous, I take a deep breath.","Saad is reliable. He always arrives early.","Noura loves writing, and she wants to be an author.","I didn't call you because my phone was dead."],"common_errors":["✗ I like math it is my favorite subject. → ✓ I like math. It is my favorite subject. (Run-on → make two sentences.)","✗ She is creative, she paints every day. → ✓ She is creative, and she paints every day. (Comma splice → add a conjunction.)","✗ He was tired he went to bed early. → ✓ He was tired, so he went to bed early. (Run-on → comma + so.)","✗ My friend is honest and he is kind and he is funny and he helps everyone. → ✓ My friend is honest, kind and funny. He helps everyone. (Too many \"ands\" – make it clearer.)"],"arabic":"الجملة المتصلة الخاطئة (run-on) تربط جملتين دون علامة ترقيم، وجملة الفاصلة الخاطئة (comma splice) تربطهما بفاصلة فقط.\nالتصحيح: نقطة بين الجملتين، أو فاصلة مع and/but/so، أو كلمة ربط مثل because وwhen.\nفي العربية نربط أفكارًا كثيرة بالواو، أما في الإنجليزية فنكتب جملًا واضحة ومنفصلة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Too Many Ideas in One Sentence: Fixing Run-On Sentences”. Let’s learn sentence boundaries: run-on sentences and comma splices; fixing them with a period, a comma + conjunction, or a subordinating word together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U1-LS4 | Too Many Ideas in One Sentence: Fixing Run-On Sentences","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A run-on sentence joins two complete sentences with no punctuation: (not: I love reading I read every night.) A comma splice joins them with only a comma: (not: I love reading, I read every night.) Both are mistakes.","on_screen":"sentence boundaries: run-on sentences and comma splices; fixing them with a period, a comma + conjunction, or a subordinating word","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A run-on sentence joins two complete sentences with no punctuation: (not: I love reading I read every night.) A comma splice joins them with only a comma: (not: I love reading, I read every night.) Both are mistakes. Fix 1 – make two sentences: I love reading. I read every night. Fix 2 – comma + and/but/or/so: I love reading, so I read every night. Fix 3 – use a joining word like because, when, although, if: I read every night because I love reading.","on_screen":"Run-on: two sentences with no punctuation → wrong • Comma splice: two sentences with only a comma → wrong • Fix: period • comma + and/but/or/so • because/when/although/if","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Lina is cheerful. She smiles all the time. Rakan is shy, but he is very funny with his friends. I stayed home because I was sick.","on_screen":"Lina is cheerful. She smiles all the time. / Rakan is shy, but he is very funny with his friends. / I stayed home because I was sick.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I like math it is my favorite subject.” That’s not right. We say: “I like math. It is my favorite subject.” Run-on → make two sentences.","on_screen":"✗ I like math it is my favorite subject.   ✓ I like math. It is my favorite subject.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"I was hungry I ate a sandwich.\" What is wrong? … Think! … It's a run-on – two sentences with no punctuation. Great job! Now you can say: I can find run-on sentences in my writing.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can find run-on sentences in my writing.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: sentence boundaries: run-on sentences and comma splices; fixing them with a period, a comma + conjunction, or a subordinating word.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الجملة المتصلة الخاطئة (run-on) تربط جملتين دون علامة ترقيم، وجملة الفاصلة الخاطئة (comma splice) تربطهما بفاصلة فقط.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I like math it is my favorite subject. — الصحيح: I like math. It is my favorite subject.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أجد الجمل المتصلة الخاطئة في كتابتي."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"About My Brother (editing passage)","body":"My brother Ziyad is fifteen he is very ambitious. He wants to study medicine so he studies every evening. He's a bit stubborn, he never changes his mind! He has a great sense of humor and he makes us laugh at dinner.","word_count":42,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["I love science, it's my favorite subject.","I love science. It's my favorite subject.","I love, science it's my favorite subject.","I love science it's my favorite subject."],"answer":"I love science. It's my favorite subject.","explanation":"Fix with a period: two sentences.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بالنقطة."},{"q":"","options":["Omar was tired he slept early.","Omar was tired, he slept early.","Omar was tired so, he slept early.","Omar was tired, so he slept early."],"answer":"Omar was tired, so he slept early.","explanation":"Fix with a comma + and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بفاصلة وأداة ربط."},{"q":"","options":["We stayed inside because it was raining.","We stayed inside it was raining.","We stayed inside, because, it was raining.","We stayed inside, it was raining."],"answer":"We stayed inside because it was raining.","explanation":"Fix with because/when/although/if.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بكلمة ربط تابعة."},{"q":"","options":["Lina is shy she's very kind.","Lina is shy, but she's very kind.","Lina is shy but, she's very kind.","Lina is shy, she's very kind."],"answer":"Lina is shy, but she's very kind.","explanation":"Fix with a comma + and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بفاصلة وأداة ربط."},{"q":"Which sentence is a comma splice?","options":["\"My brother is funny, and he makes everyone laugh.\"","\"My brother is funny. He makes everyone laugh.\"","\"My brother makes everyone laugh because he is funny.\"","\"My brother is funny, he makes everyone laugh.\""],"answer":"\"My brother is funny, he makes everyone laugh.\"","explanation":"Two sentences with only a comma = comma splice.","explanation_ar":"جملتان بفاصلة فقط = comma splice."},{"q":"Which sentence is a run-on?","options":["\"I finished my homework. I watched TV.\"","\"After I finished my homework, I watched TV.\"","\"I finished my homework I watched TV.\"","\"I finished my homework, and I watched TV.\""],"answer":"\"I finished my homework I watched TV.\"","explanation":"Two sentences with no punctuation = run-on.","explanation_ar":"جملتان بلا ترقيم = run-on."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Fix the run-on or comma splice. Use the word in brackets.","items":[{"q":"Faisal is ambitious  +  he wants to be a pilot (and)","options":[],"answer":"Faisal is ambitious, and he wants to be a pilot.","explanation":"Fix with a comma + and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بفاصلة وأداة ربط."},{"q":"The test was hard  +  I passed it (but)","options":[],"answer":"The test was hard, but I passed it.","explanation":"Fix with a comma + and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بفاصلة وأداة ربط."},{"q":"I couldn't sleep  +  I was worried about the match (because)","options":[],"answer":"I couldn't sleep because I was worried about the match.","explanation":"Fix with because/when/although/if.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بكلمة ربط تابعة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS4-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Fix with a period. Write two sentences.","items":[{"q":"My cousin is creative she designs her own clothes.  (two sentences)","options":[],"answer":"My cousin is creative. She designs her own clothes.","explanation":"Fix with a period: two sentences.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بالنقطة."},{"q":"The new student is sociable, everyone likes him.  (two sentences)","options":[],"answer":"The new student is sociable. Everyone likes him.","explanation":"Fix with a period: two sentences.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بالنقطة."},{"q":"I'm learning to code it's difficult but fun.  (two sentences)","options":[],"answer":"I'm learning to code. It's difficult but fun.","explanation":"Fix with a period: two sentences.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بالنقطة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the profile.","items":[{"q":"My brother Ziyad is fifteen He is very ambitious.","options":[],"answer":"My brother Ziyad is fifteen. He is very ambitious.","explanation":"(add) → .. Two sentences with no punctuation = run-on.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → .. جملتان بلا ترقيم = run-on."},{"q":"My brother Ziyad is fifteen. he is very ambitious.","options":[],"answer":"My brother Ziyad is fifteen. He is very ambitious.","explanation":"he → He. Two sentences with no punctuation = run-on.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: he → He. جملتان بلا ترقيم = run-on."},{"q":"He wants to study medicine so he studies every evening.","options":[],"answer":"He wants to study medicine, so he studies every evening.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Two sentences with no punctuation = run-on.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملتان بلا ترقيم = run-on."},{"q":"He's a bit stubborn, He never changes his mind!","options":[],"answer":"He's a bit stubborn. He never changes his mind!","explanation":", → .. Two sentences with no punctuation = run-on.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → .. جملتان بلا ترقيم = run-on."},{"q":"My brother Ziyad is fifteen. he is very ambitious.","options":[],"answer":"My brother Ziyad is fifteen. He is very ambitious.","explanation":"he → He. Two sentences with no punctuation = run-on.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: he → He. جملتان بلا ترقيم = run-on."},{"q":"He wants to study medicine so he studies every evening.","options":[],"answer":"He wants to study medicine, so he studies every evening.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Two sentences with no punctuation = run-on.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملتان بلا ترقيم = run-on."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write clear sentences.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences about a friend's personality joined with a comma + but.","options":[],"answer":"My friend is quiet, but he's very confident in class.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses sentence boundaries: run-on sentences and comma splices; fixing them with a period, a comma + conjunction, or a subordinating word correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with because about why you like a hobby.","options":[],"answer":"I like drawing because it helps me relax.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses sentence boundaries: run-on sentences and comma splices; fixing them with a period, a comma + conjunction, or a subordinating word correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Take this run-on and fix it in two different ways: \"I was late the bus didn't come.\"","options":[],"answer":"I was late. The bus didn't come. / I was late because the bus didn't come.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses sentence boundaries: run-on sentences and comma splices; fixing them with a period, a comma + conjunction, or a subordinating word correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Letter Ladder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The leader chooses a word from the list and draws one blank line per letter.","Teams take turns guessing letters. Correct letters are written on the lines.","Each wrong guess removes one rung of the ladder (start with 6 rungs).","The team that completes the word scores 2 points and uses it in a sentence."],"data":[{"word":"personality","clue":"the way a person usually thinks, feels and behaves"},{"word":"confident","clue":"sure of yourself and your abilities"},{"word":"curious","clue":"wanting to know or learn about things"},{"word":"reliable","clue":"someone you can trust to do what they say"},{"word":"ambitious","clue":"wanting very much to succeed"},{"word":"sociable","clue":"enjoying being with other people"},{"word":"shy","clue":"nervous about talking to people you don't know"},{"word":"honest","clue":"always telling the truth"},{"word":"patient","clue":"able to wait calmly without getting angry"},{"word":"creative","clue":"good at making new things and ideas"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["Adam is creative, he builds robots.","Adam is creative. He builds robots.","Adam is creative, he, builds robots.","Adam is creative he builds robots."],"answer":"Adam is creative. He builds robots.","explanation":"Fix with a period: two sentences.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بالنقطة."},{"q":"","options":["I was hungry, I made a sandwich.","I was hungry so, I made a sandwich.","I was hungry I made a sandwich.","I was hungry, so I made a sandwich."],"answer":"I was hungry, so I made a sandwich.","explanation":"Fix with a comma + and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بفاصلة وأداة ربط."},{"q":"How can we fix \"It's late I'm going to bed.\"?","options":["It's late, so I'm going to bed.","It's, late I'm going to bed.","It's late I'm going, to bed.","It's late, I'm going to bed."],"answer":"It's late, so I'm going to bed.","explanation":"Fix with a comma + and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بفاصلة وأداة ربط."},{"q":"","options":["I feel stressed I go for a walk.","When I feel stressed I go, for a walk.","When I feel stressed, I go for a walk.","I feel stressed, I go for a walk."],"answer":"When I feel stressed, I go for a walk.","explanation":"Fix with because/when/although/if.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بكلمة ربط تابعة."},{"q":"What is the problem with \"Sara is honest, she never lies.\"?","options":["It needs a question mark.","Nothing is wrong.","It's a comma splice.","It's a fragment."],"answer":"It's a comma splice.","explanation":"Two sentences with only a comma = comma splice.","explanation_ar":"جملتان بفاصلة فقط = comma splice."},{"q":"","options":["My sister is sociable, she has many friends.","My sister is sociable, and she has many friends.","My sister is sociable she has many friends.","My sister is sociable and, she has many friends."],"answer":"My sister is sociable, and she has many friends.","explanation":"Fix with a comma + and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بفاصلة وأداة ربط."},{"q":"","options":["He didn't come to school because he was sick.","He didn't come to school he was sick.","He didn't come to school, he was sick.","He didn't come to school because, he was sick."],"answer":"He didn't come to school because he was sick.","explanation":"Fix with because/when/although/if.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بكلمة ربط تابعة."},{"q":"","options":["My grandpa is wise everyone asks him for advice.","My grandpa is, wise everyone asks him for advice.","My grandpa is wise, everyone asks him for advice.","My grandpa is wise. Everyone asks him for advice."],"answer":"My grandpa is wise. Everyone asks him for advice.","explanation":"Fix with a period: two sentences.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بالنقطة."},{"q":"Which word can fix a run-on?","options":["very","quickly","because","the"],"answer":"because","explanation":"Fix with because/when/although/if.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بكلمة ربط تابعة."},{"q":"","options":["Rakan is shy, but he speaks well in class.","Rakan is shy he speaks well in class.","Rakan is shy but, he speaks well in class.","Rakan is shy, he speaks well in class."],"answer":"Rakan is shy, but he speaks well in class.","explanation":"Fix with a comma + and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بفاصلة وأداة ربط."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Who Am I?” that shows sentence boundaries: run-on sentences and comma splices; fixing them with a period, a comma + conjunction, or a subordinating word in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Who Am I?” that shows sentence boundaries: run-on sentences and comma splices; fixing them with a period, a comma + conjunction, or a subordinating word in action"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Letter Ladder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Letter Ladder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Too Many Ideas in One Sentence: Fixing Run-On Sentences”. Let’s learn sentence boundaries: run-on sentences and comma splices; fixing them with a period, a comma + conjunction, or a subordinating word together. A run-on sentence joins two complete sentences with no punctuation: (not: I love reading I read every night.) A comma splice joins them with only a comma: (not: I love reading, I read every night.) Both are mistakes. A run-on sentence joins two complete sentences with no punctuation: (not: I love reading I read every night.) A comma splice joins them with only a comma: (not: I love reading, I read every night.) Both are mistakes. Fix 1 – make two sentences: I love reading. I read every night. Fix 2 – comma + and/but/or/so: I love reading, so I read every night. Fix 3 – use a joining word like because, when, although, if: I read every night because I love reading. Here are some examples. Lina is cheerful. She smiles all the time. Rakan is shy, but he is very funny with his friends. I stayed home because I was sick. Be careful! Some learners say: “I like math it is my favorite subject.” That’s not right. We say: “I like math. It is my favorite subject.” Run-on → make two sentences. Quick check: \"I was hungry I ate a sandwich.\" What is wrong? … Think! … It's a run-on – two sentences with no punctuation. Great job! Now you can say: I can find run-on sentences in my writing.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS5","title":"My Personal Profile: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to introduce themselves and a classmate using habits, current activities and personality words.","Students will be able to write a personal profile with correct tenses and no run-on sentences.","I can introduce a classmate to the class.","I can write my personal profile for the school magazine."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تقديم أنفسهم وزميل لهم بالعادات والأنشطة الحالية وصفات الشخصية.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة ملف شخصي بأزمنة صحيحة ودون جمل متصلة خاطئة.","أستطيع أن أقدّم زميلًا للصف.","أستطيع أن أكتب ملفي الشخصي لمجلة المدرسة."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"personality","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌpɝsəˈnælɪti/","definition":"the way a person usually thinks, feels and behaves","arabic":"شخصية","example":"Lina has a warm and friendly personality.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"confident","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkɑnfədənt/","definition":"sure of yourself and your abilities","arabic":"واثق من نفسه","example":"Saad looks confident when he speaks in public.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"shy","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ʃaɪ/","definition":"nervous about talking to people you don't know","arabic":"خجول","example":"My little brother is shy with new people.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"curious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈkjʊriəs/","definition":"wanting to know or learn about things","arabic":"فضولي / محب للمعرفة","example":"Curious students ask a lot of questions.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"honest","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈɑnəst/","definition":"always telling the truth","arabic":"صادق / أمين","example":"An honest person doesn't cheat.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"patient","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpeɪʃənt/","definition":"able to wait calmly without getting angry","arabic":"صبور","example":"A good teacher is patient with every student.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"reliable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/rɪˈlaɪəbəl/","definition":"someone you can trust to do what they say","arabic":"يُعتمد عليه","example":"Ziyad is reliable – he's never late.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ambitious","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/æmˈbɪʃəs/","definition":"wanting very much to succeed","arabic":"طموح","example":"Rakan is ambitious; he wants to be a surgeon.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sociable","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsoʊʃəbəl/","definition":"enjoying being with other people","arabic":"اجتماعي","example":"Sociable people make friends easily.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"creative","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/kriˈeɪtɪv/","definition":"good at making new things and ideas","arabic":"مبدع","example":"Noura is creative – she writes amazing stories.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"calm","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/kɑm/","definition":"quiet and not worried or angry","arabic":"هادئ","example":"Stay calm and read the question again.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"stubborn","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈstʌbɚn/","definition":"not willing to change your mind","arabic":"عنيد","example":"My grandpa is stubborn about his old phone.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sense of humor","pos":"noun phrase","ipa":"/sɛns ʌv ˈhjumɚ/","definition":"the ability to see and enjoy funny things","arabic":"حس الفكاهة","example":"Adam has a great sense of humor.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"character","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɛrɪktɚ/","definition":"the qualities that make a person who they are","arabic":"طبع / شخصية","example":"Helping others shows good character.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 1: the present simple and continuous, state verbs, always + -ing, personality words with prefixes and clear sentence boundaries.\nA profile describes who someone is (personality, likes – simple), what he usually does (habits – simple) and what he's doing these days (projects – continuous).\n✔ simple: habits, facts, likes (state verbs)\n✔ continuous: now, these days, this term\n✔ personality words + prefixes (impatient, disorganized)\n✔ no run-ons: period / comma + conjunction / because","examples":["Ziyad lives in Jeddah and loves the sea.","These days, he's training for a swimming competition.","He's very sociable, so he has lots of friends.","He believes that hard work is important.","He's always helping his younger brothers.","He's a bit disorganized, but he's improving.","He doesn't like waiting in long lines.","His friends think he's reliable."],"common_errors":["✗ He is liking football very much. → ✓ He likes football very much. (State verb → simple.)","✗ This term he builds a robot. → ✓ This term, he's building a robot. (Temporary project → continuous.)","✗ He's honest he never lies. → ✓ He's honest. He never lies. / He's honest, so he never lies. (Fix the run-on.)"],"arabic":"نراجع المضارع البسيط والمستمر وأفعال الحالة وصفات الشخصية والبادئات وحدود الجملة.\nالملف الشخصي يصف: مَن هو (صفات وحب – بسيط)، وماذا يفعل عادة (بسيط)، وماذا يفعل هذه الأيام (مستمر).\nتذكّر: لا جمل متصلة خاطئة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Personal Profile: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L05-U1-LS5 | My Personal Profile: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Introduce your partner: interview a partner about his personality, habits, current projects and one thing he's always doing (good or annoying). Then introduce him to the class in 6 sentences.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 1: the present simple and continuous, state verbs, always + -ing, personality words with prefixes and clear sentence boundaries. A profile describes who someone is (personality, likes – simple), what he usually does (habits – simple) and what he's doing these days (projects – continuous).","on_screen":"✔ simple: habits, facts, likes (state verbs) • ✔ continuous: now, these days, this term • ✔ personality words + prefixes (impatient, disorganized)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Ziyad lives in Jeddah and loves the sea. These days, he's training for a swimming competition. He's very sociable, so he has lots of friends.","on_screen":"Ziyad lives in Jeddah and loves the sea. / These days, he's training for a swimming competition. / He's very sociable, so he has lots of friends.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He is liking football very much.” That’s not right. We say: “He likes football very much.” State verb → simple.","on_screen":"✗ He is liking football very much.   ✓ He likes football very much.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “This term he builds a robot.”? … Think! … It should be “This term, he's building a robot.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can introduce a classmate to the class.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can introduce a classmate to the class.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع المضارع البسيط والمستمر وأفعال الحالة وصفات الشخصية والبادئات وحدود الجملة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He is liking football very much. — الصحيح: He likes football very much.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقدّم زميلًا للصف."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Meet Omar – School Magazine","body":"Omar is thirteen, and he lives in Taif with his family.\nHe's curious and confident, and he loves science and football.\nHe usually plays football with his cousins on Thursday evenings.\nThis term, he's building a weather station for the science fair, so he's spending a lot of time in the lab.\nHis friends say he's reliable because he never forgets a promise.\nHe admits that he's sometimes impatient, but he's working on it.\nHe wants to become an engineer one day.","word_count":82,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Omar's profile. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Omar lives in Taif with his family.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Meet Omar – School Magazine”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Omar is shy and quiet.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Meet Omar – School Magazine”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Omar usually plays football on Thursday evenings.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Meet Omar – School Magazine”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"This term, Omar is building a weather station.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Meet Omar – School Magazine”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"His friends say he often forgets his promises.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Meet Omar – School Magazine”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Omar admits that he's sometimes impatient.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Meet Omar – School Magazine”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"Omar usually ___ football with his cousins.","options":["playing","is playing","play","plays"],"answer":"plays","explanation":"Habit, fact or state verb → present simple.","explanation_ar":"البسيط."},{"q":"This term, he ___ a weather station.","options":["builds","is building","building","build"],"answer":"is building","explanation":"These days / this term / now → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"المستمر."},{"q":"He never forgets a promise. He's ___.","options":["shy","unreliable","stubborn","reliable"],"answer":"reliable","explanation":"Personality word or prefix.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية."},{"q":"He's sometimes ___, but he's working on it.","options":["dispatient","unpatient","impatient","inpatient"],"answer":"impatient","explanation":"Personality word or prefix.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية."},{"q":"","options":["He wants to become an engineer.","He want to become an engineer.","He wanting to become an engineer.","He is wanting to become an engineer."],"answer":"He wants to become an engineer.","explanation":"State verb in the simple form.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحالة."},{"q":"","options":["He's curious. He asks a lot of questions.","He's curious he asks a lot of questions.","He's curious, he asks a lot of questions.","He's curious, he, asks a lot of questions."],"answer":"He's curious. He asks a lot of questions.","explanation":"Correct sentence boundary (no run-on, no comma splice).","explanation_ar":"حدود الجملة."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Interview your partner. Write his answers.","items":[{"q":"Ask about his personality (3 adjectives).","options":[],"answer":"He says he's calm, curious and a bit stubborn.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask about his usual weekend.","options":[],"answer":"He usually visits his grandparents and plays video games.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask about a project he's doing these days.","options":[],"answer":"He's learning to play the oud this month.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask what someone in his family is always doing.","options":[],"answer":"His little sister is always singing!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask about his dream for the future.","options":[],"answer":"He wants to be a pilot.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your personal profile.","items":[{"q":"Plan: name, age, home, 3 personality words, 2 habits, 2 current projects, 1 dream.","options":[],"answer":"Faisal, 13, Riyadh; ambitious, sociable, disorganized; plays basketball, reads comics; training for a race, learning Spanish; to be a doctor","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your profile in 7–8 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"My name is Faisal, and I live in Riyadh. I'm ambitious and sociable. I usually play basketball after school. I also read comics before bed. These days, I'm training for a race. I'm learning Spanish too. I'm a bit disorganized, but I'm getting better. I want to be a doctor one day.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: simple vs continuous? state verbs? run-ons? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"I'm wanting to be a doctor\" to \"I want to be a doctor\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Treasure Hunt Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams move to a station every 90 seconds.","At each station, write one correct sentence with the cue word and present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review).","Teams collect a \"treasure letter\" for each correct sentence.","Unscramble the letters at the end to reveal the secret word."],"data":[{"cue":"personality","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"confident","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"shy","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"curious","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"honest","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"patient","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"reliable","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"ambitious","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sociable","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"creative","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"calm","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"stubborn","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sense of humor","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"character","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"My sister ___ to the school choir.","options":["belong","is belonging","belonging","belongs"],"answer":"belongs","explanation":"State verb in the simple form.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحالة."},{"q":"These days, I ___ to wake up earlier.","options":["tries","am trying","trying","try"],"answer":"am trying","explanation":"These days / this term / now → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"المستمر."},{"q":"My uncle ___ in a hospital. He's a nurse.","options":["working","work","works","is working this week"],"answer":"works","explanation":"Habit, fact or state verb → present simple.","explanation_ar":"البسيط."},{"q":"Someone who is not organized is ___.","options":["disorganized","imorganized","inorganized","unorganized"],"answer":"disorganized","explanation":"Personality word or prefix.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية."},{"q":"","options":["My cousin is telling always funny stories!","My cousin always is telling funny stories!","My cousin is always tell funny stories!","My cousin is always telling funny stories!"],"answer":"My cousin is always telling funny stories!","explanation":"These days / this term / now → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["Saad is ambitious he wants to win every competition.","Saad is ambitious. He wants to win every competition.","Saad is ambitious, he, wants to win every competition.","Saad is ambitious, he wants to win every competition."],"answer":"Saad is ambitious. He wants to win every competition.","explanation":"Correct sentence boundary (no run-on, no comma splice).","explanation_ar":"حدود الجملة."},{"q":"","options":["I understanding the lesson now.","I'm understanding the lesson now.","I understand the lesson now.","I am understand the lesson now."],"answer":"I understand the lesson now.","explanation":"State verb in the simple form.","explanation_ar":"فعل الحالة."},{"q":"Hamad tells the truth. He is ___.","options":["impolite","honest","dishonest","stubborn"],"answer":"honest","explanation":"Personality word or prefix.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية."},{"q":"","options":["Lina loves art, so she's taking a painting course this month.","Lina is loving art, so she takes a painting course this month.","Lina loves art she's taking a painting course this month.","Lina loves art, she's taking a painting course this month."],"answer":"Lina loves art, so she's taking a painting course this month.","explanation":"Correct sentence boundary (no run-on, no comma splice).","explanation_ar":"حدود الجملة."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a personal profile:","options":["I usually calm, but these days I'm nervous about exams.","I'm usually calm but these days I feel nervous about exams I study a lot.","I'm being usually calm, but these days I feel nervous.","I'm usually calm, but these days I'm feeling nervous about exams."],"answer":"I'm usually calm, but these days I'm feeling nervous about exams.","explanation":"These days / this term / now → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"المستمر."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"The school magazine page \"Meet Our Students\" with photos and short profiles, Yusuf interviewing Omar with a notebook. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"The school magazine page \"Meet Our Students\" with photos and short profiles, Yusuf interviewing Omar with a notebook"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Who Am I?”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as young teenagers aged 12–14, slightly more detailed, energetic composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Who Am I?”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L05-U1-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Treasure Hunt Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Treasure Hunt Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS5-T1","script":"Omar is thirteen, and he lives in Taif with his family. He's curious and confident, and he loves science and football. He usually plays football with his cousins on Thursday evenings. This term, he's building a weather station for the science fair, so he's spending a lot of time in the lab. His friends say he's reliable because he never forgets a promise. He admits that he's sometimes impatient, but he's working on it. He wants to become an engineer one day.","voice":"en-US, friendly young-adult voice","speed":"0.95"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L05-U1-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “My Personal Profile: Language in Use”. Let’s learn present simple vs continuous, state verbs, personality words with prefixes, sentence boundaries (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Introduce your partner: interview a partner about his personality, habits, current projects and one thing he's always doing (good or annoying). Then introduce him to the class in 6 sentences. Today you use all of Unit 1: the present simple and continuous, state verbs, always + -ing, personality words with prefixes and clear sentence boundaries. A profile describes who someone is (personality, likes – simple), what he usually does (habits – simple) and what he's doing these days (projects – continuous). Here are some examples. Ziyad lives in Jeddah and loves the sea. These days, he's training for a swimming competition. He's very sociable, so he has lots of friends. Be careful! Some learners say: “He is liking football very much.” That’s not right. We say: “He likes football very much.” State verb → simple. Quick check: what is wrong with “This term he builds a robot.”? … Think! … It should be “This term, he's building a robot.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can introduce a classmate to the class.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.95"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"My cousin ___ three languages.","options":["speaking","speaks","speak","is speaking"],"answer":"speaks","explanation":"Habit, routine, fact or permanent situation → present simple.","explanation_ar":"العادة أو الحقيقة ← المضارع البسيط."},{"q":"Shh! The teacher ___.","options":["talks","is talk","talk","is talking"],"answer":"is talking","explanation":"Now or temporary (these days, this month) → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الآن أو المؤقت ← المضارع المستمر."},{"q":"Do you ___ this word?","options":["understanding","understands","understand","are understanding"],"answer":"understand","explanation":"State verbs (know, like, want, belong, understand) → simple form.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"This month, my dad ___ from home.","options":["work","is working","working","works"],"answer":"is working","explanation":"Temporary situation → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الوضع المؤقت ← المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["We has a house near the sea.","We having a house near the sea.","We are having a house near the sea.","We have a house near the sea."],"answer":"We have a house near the sea.","explanation":"have = own (simple) / eat, take, enjoy (continuous).","explanation_ar":"have بمعنيين."},{"q":"","options":["Riyadh is get bigger every year.","Riyadh getting bigger every year.","Riyadh is getting bigger every year.","Riyadh gets bigger these days now."],"answer":"Riyadh is getting bigger every year.","explanation":"Changing situation (getting, becoming, growing) → continuous.","explanation_ar":"التغيّر ← المستمر."},{"q":"","options":["My brother always is leaving his shoes in the hall!","My brother is always leave his shoes in the hall!","My brother is leaving always his shoes in the hall!","My brother is always leaving his shoes in the hall!"],"answer":"My brother is always leaving his shoes in the hall!","explanation":"always + -ing = annoying habit.","explanation_ar":"always + ing للعادة المزعجة."},{"q":"I ___ about studying abroad next year.","options":["am thinking","thinking","thinks","think"],"answer":"am thinking","explanation":"think = opinion (simple) / considering (continuous).","explanation_ar":"think بمعنيين."},{"q":"The Moon ___ around the Earth.","options":["is going","goes","go","going"],"answer":"goes","explanation":"Permanent situation → present simple.","explanation_ar":"الوضع الدائم ← البسيط."},{"q":"Which sentence uses a state verb correctly?","options":["I preferring tea to coffee.","I prefer tea to coffee.","I'm preferring tea to coffee.","I am prefer tea to coffee."],"answer":"I prefer tea to coffee.","explanation":"State verbs (know, like, want, belong, understand) → simple form.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"Someone who is never nervous in front of people is ___.","options":["impatient","shy","stubborn","confident"],"answer":"confident","explanation":"Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"Someone who won't change his mind is ___.","options":["stubborn","curious","calm","sociable"],"answer":"stubborn","explanation":"Choose the personality word that matches the description.","explanation_ar":"صفة الشخصية المناسبة."},{"q":"The opposite of \"mature\" is ___.","options":["dismature","unmature","immature","inmature"],"answer":"immature","explanation":"im- before p or m (impatient, impolite).","explanation_ar":"im قبل p وm."},{"q":"The opposite of \"honest\" is ___.","options":["dishonest","imhonest","unhonest","inhonest"],"answer":"dishonest","explanation":"dis- + adjective (dishonest, disorganized).","explanation_ar":"البادئة dis."},{"q":"The opposite of \"reliable\" is ___.","options":["unreliable","inreliable","imreliable","disreliable"],"answer":"unreliable","explanation":"un- + adjective.","explanation_ar":"البادئة un."},{"q":"The opposite of \"sensitive\" is ___.","options":["dissensitive","imsensitive","insensitive","unsensitive"],"answer":"insensitive","explanation":"in- + adjective (insensitive, inconsiderate).","explanation_ar":"البادئة in."},{"q":"","options":["Ziyad is creative he makes his own games.","Ziyad is creative, he, makes his own games.","Ziyad is creative, he makes his own games.","Ziyad is creative. He makes his own games."],"answer":"Ziyad is creative. He makes his own games.","explanation":"Fix with a period: two sentences.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بالنقطة."},{"q":"","options":["I was nervous, I took a deep breath.","I was nervous so, I took a deep breath.","I was nervous, so I took a deep breath.","I was nervous I took a deep breath."],"answer":"I was nervous, so I took a deep breath.","explanation":"Fix with a comma + and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بفاصلة وأداة ربط."},{"q":"","options":["She smiled because she was happy.","She smiled she was happy.","She smiled because, she was happy.","She smiled, she was happy."],"answer":"She smiled because she was happy.","explanation":"Fix with because/when/although/if.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بكلمة ربط تابعة."},{"q":"What is the problem with \"My friend is kind, he helps everyone.\"?","options":["It's a fragment.","It's missing a capital letter.","It's a comma splice.","Nothing is wrong."],"answer":"It's a comma splice.","explanation":"Two sentences with only a comma = comma splice.","explanation_ar":"جملتان بفاصلة فقط = comma splice."},{"q":"Find the run-on sentence.","options":["\"I love my school, and I have great friends there.\"","\"I love my school I have great friends there.\"","\"I love my school. I have great friends there.\"","\"I love my school because I have great friends there.\""],"answer":"\"I love my school I have great friends there.\"","explanation":"Two sentences with no punctuation = run-on.","explanation_ar":"جملتان بلا ترقيم = run-on."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a profile:","options":["Faisal is being calm and reliable, so his teammates are trusting him.","Faisal is calm and reliable, so his teammates trust him.","Faisal is calm and reliable his teammates trust him.","Faisal is calm and reliable, his teammates trust him."],"answer":"Faisal is calm and reliable, so his teammates trust him.","explanation":"Fix with a comma + and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح بفاصلة وأداة ربط."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"i am knowing her she is my neighbor.\"","options":["I know her she is my neighbor.","i know her, she is my neighbor.","I am knowing her. She is my neighbor.","I know her. She is my neighbor."],"answer":"I know her. She is my neighbor.","explanation":"State verbs (know, like, want, belong, understand) → simple form.","explanation_ar":"أفعال الحالة ← البسيط."},{"q":"What are you doing these days? – ___","options":["I'm preparing for a math competition.","I prepare for a math competition now.","I'm prepare for a math competition.","I preparing for a math competition."],"answer":"I'm preparing for a math competition.","explanation":"Now or temporary (these days, this month) → present continuous.","explanation_ar":"الآن أو المؤقت ← المضارع المستمر."}],"theme_ar":"مَن أنا؟","essential_question_ar":"ما الذي يجعل كل شخص فريدًا؟","can_do":"I can describe my personality, habits and current activities with the present simple and present continuous, and write clear sentences without run-ons.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف شخصيتي وعاداتي وأنشطتي الحالية بالمضارع البسيط والمضارع المستمر، وأكتب جملًا واضحة دون جمل متصلة خاطئة."});
